>>Also, just to make sure I'm not crazy here, the original Russian word 
which >>you translate as {balvi} doesn't mean "future" explicitly, right?
I guess this word "dalyoko" in Russian was first introduced in Russian in 
this song. I believe it was bad grammar at that time. But now it's ok 
(probably because of this song :-) ) and it means "distant future".
So I translated it as "zu balvi". Is it correct ?

>>You are aware that the {fe} in the second line is superfluous and you did 
it >>just for rhythm, I assume.
I could use "cu" instead of "fe". I just took an unusual choice.

